  "id": "Compound::DB06701 - Gene::6531",
  "verbalization": "Dexmethylphenidate is implicated in the regulation of Slc6a3 through a shared mechanism involving Methylphenidate. Both Dexmethylphenidate and Methylphenidate bind to Slc6a3, suggesting a common interaction with the transporter. The evidence indicates that Dexmethylphenidate causes various effects, including vocal tics, chest pain, and weight gain, all of which are mediated by Methylphenidate. This suggests that the effects of Dexmethylphenidate may be mediated through Methylphenidate, which in turn interacts with Slc6a3. The presence of a common lowest common ancestor, the Nitrogen Molecular Entity, and the Cns Stimulant category further supports a shared pharmacological profile. The integration of these findings implies that Dexmethylphenidate may exert its effects through a pathway that involves Methylphenidate and Slc6a3, highlighting a potential role in the modulation of neurotransmitter transport.",
